      <h2>1. Workable</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> End-to-end recruitment for SMEs and growing agencies</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.6 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £99/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Workable is the recruitment platform that scales with your ambition. A London fintech startup used it to grow from 10 to 80 employees in 18 months, managing every role from junior developer to CFO through one system. The AI features write job descriptions, suggest candidates from a database of 400 million profiles, rank applicants by fit, and even predict which candidates will accept your offer.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI job description writer:</strong> Generate optimised job descriptions from a few bullet points. The AI ensures inclusive language, appropriate seniority levels, and SEO-friendly titles.</li>
        <li><strong>Sourcing AI:</strong> Search 400 million candidate profiles across the web. The AI suggests candidates who match your requirements but might not have applied.</li>
        <li><strong>Resume parsing and ranking:</strong> Upload 100 CVs and the AI extracts skills, experience, and qualifications, ranking candidates against your criteria in seconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Interview scheduling:</strong> Automated calendar integration finds mutually available slots across multiple interviewers and time zones.</li>
        <li><strong>Collaborative hiring:</strong> Scorecards, feedback forms, and structured evaluation criteria ensure every interviewer assesses consistently.</li>
        <li><strong>Offer management:</strong> Generate offer letters, track acceptance rates, and analyse which offers succeed and why.</li>
        <li><strong>Reporting and analytics:</strong> Pipeline velocity, source effectiveness, diversity metrics, and cost-per-hire dashboards.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The AI sourcing is genuinely effective. One agency sourced three qualified candidates for a niche DevOps role in 24 hours</li>
        <li>Job description writer produces inclusive, professional copy that attracts diverse applicants</li>
        <li>The collaborative scoring system reduces bias by standardising evaluation criteria</li>
        <li>Integration with 200+ job boards means one-click posting across Indeed, LinkedIn, NHS Jobs, and specialist boards</li>
        <li>Customer support includes live chat with recruiters who understand the hiring process</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £99/month for the Starter plan, it is an investment for agencies placing fewer than 10 roles per month</li>
        <li>The AI ranking occasionally misses context. A candidate with non-linear career progression may score poorly despite being ideal</li>
        <li>Advanced analytics require the Professional plan (£299/month). Starter reporting is basic</li>
        <li>Some users report the mobile app lacks features available on desktop, forcing managers back to their laptops</li>
        <li>Integration with some UK payroll systems requires middleware or manual exports</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate Workable 4.5/5, calling it "the most complete recruitment platform for growing companies." A Trustpilot reviewer from a Bristol SaaS company said the AI sourcing "found candidates we would never have discovered through traditional advertising." Reddit users on r/recruitment praise the collaborative features but note the AI job descriptions need human editing to avoid sounding generic.</p>

      <h3>Pricing</h3>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Starter</td><td>£99/month</td><td>2 active jobs, AI sourcing, basic reporting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Professional</td><td>£299/month</td><td>20 active jobs, advanced analytics, video interviews</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Enterprise</td><td>Custom</td><td>Unlimited jobs, API access, custom integrations, dedicated support</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> Editor's Choice for all-round recruitment. Workable is the platform we recommend when someone asks "what recruitment software should I buy?" It balances power with usability and scales from your first hire to your hundredth.</p>
      <p><a href="https://workable.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start a free trial with Workable</a> (affiliate link)</p>

      <h2>2. Hiretual (HireEZ)</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Talent sourcing, Boolean search, and candidate pipeline building</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.5 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £125/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Hiretual (recently rebranded as HireEZ) is the sourcing engine that powers the best recruitment agencies. A specialist healthcare recruiter in Birmingham uses it to build pipelines of qualified nurses, care workers, and allied health professionals before vacancies even arise. The AI searches across LinkedIn, GitHub, Stack Overflow, NHS staff directories, and dozens of other sources to find candidates who match your precise criteria.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI sourcing assistant:</strong> Describe your ideal candidate in natural language. "Find me a band 6 mental health nurse with CBT training within 50 miles of Manchester" generates a targeted candidate list in seconds.</li>
        <li><strong>Boolean builder:</strong> Create complex search strings with a visual interface. No need to memorise Boolean operators.</li>
        <li><strong>Candidate enrichment:</strong> Automatically populate candidate profiles with contact details, skills, and work history from across the web.</li>
        <li><strong>Diversity sourcing:</strong> AI features that help you build diverse shortlists by expanding your search beyond traditional networks.</li>
        <li><strong>Pipeline management:</strong> Organise candidates into projects, stages, and talent pools. Nurture relationships before roles open.</li>
        <li><strong>Engagement automation:</strong> Schedule personalised outreach sequences across email, LinkedIn, and InMail.</li>
        <li><strong>Market insights:</strong> Analyse talent supply, demand, and salary benchmarks for any role in any location.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The AI sourcing is the most powerful available. Finds candidates that LinkedIn Recruiter misses</li>
        <li>Boolean builder makes complex sourcing accessible to junior recruiters</li>
        <li>Candidate enrichment saves hours of manual profile building</li>
        <li>Diversity sourcing features genuinely expand candidate pools beyond traditional networks</li>
        <li>Market insights help you advise clients on realistic salary expectations and availability</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £125/month, it is a specialist tool. Generalist recruiters may not use its full capability</li>
        <li>The interface is powerful but complex. Expect 2-4 weeks of training before full proficiency</li>
        <li>Contact data accuracy varies by industry. Healthcare and tech are strong; creative industries are weaker</li>
        <li>Engagement automation can feel impersonal if overused. Balance AI efficiency with human touch</li>
        <li>Some users report data freshness issues. Candidates who changed jobs six months ago may still show old employers</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate HireEZ 4.4/5, calling it "the sourcing tool that separates good recruiters from great ones." A Trustpilot reviewer from a healthcare staffing agency said the AI sourcing "cut our time-to-fill by 40% for hard-to-fill nursing roles." The main complaint: the rebrand from Hiretual to HireEZ caused some confusion and integration issues that took months to resolve.</p>

      <h3>Pricing</h3>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Starter</td><td>£125/month</td><td>3 user seats, AI sourcing, basic enrichment</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Professional</td><td>£250/month</td><td>10 user seats, advanced analytics, engagement automation</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Enterprise</td><td>Custom</td><td>Unlimited seats, API access, custom integrations, dedicated support</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> Editor's Choice for talent sourcing. If sourcing passive candidates is a significant part of your recruitment strategy, HireEZ is essential. For agencies that rely on inbound applications, Workable's built-in sourcing may be sufficient.</p>
      <p><a href="https://hireez.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start sourcing with HireEZ</a> (affiliate link)</p>

      <h2>3. HireVue</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Video interviewing, assessment, and candidate experience</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.4 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Custom pricing (typically £5,000-£15,000/year)</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>HireVue transformed the first-round interview from a scheduling nightmare into a scalable assessment process. A national retailer with 200 stores uses it to interview 5,000 seasonal candidates in two weeks, assessing communication skills, problem-solving ability, and cultural fit through structured video responses. The AI analyses verbal responses, facial expressions, and language patterns to identify candidates who match the profiles of top performers.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>On-demand video interviews:</strong> Candidates record responses at their convenience. Review at 2x speed, share with hiring managers, and compare side-by-side.</li>
        <li><strong>Live video interviews:</strong> Structured live interviews with integrated assessment tools and real-time scoring.</li>
        <li><strong>AI-powered assessments:</strong> Game-based assessments that measure cognitive ability, emotional intelligence, and job-specific skills without bias-prone CV screening.</li>
        <li><strong>Interview analytics:</strong> AI analyses responses for communication clarity, confidence, and content relevance. Identify candidates who interview well but lack substance.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured evaluation:</strong> Standardised scorecards ensure every candidate is assessed against the same criteria. Reduce unconscious bias.</li>
        <li><strong>Candidate experience:</strong> Mobile-friendly interface with practice questions and clear instructions. First impressions matter.</li>
        <li><strong>Integration:</strong> Connects with Workable, Greenhouse, SAP SuccessFactors, and most major ATS platforms.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>On-demand interviews eliminate scheduling conflicts. One recruiter can assess 50 candidates in a day</li>
        <li>The AI assessments reduce reliance on CVs, which disproportionately disadvantage non-traditional candidates</li>
        <li>Structured scoring reduces bias. One client increased diversity hires by 35% after implementing HireVue</li>
        <li>The candidate experience is polished. Applicants receive feedback and status updates automatically</li>
        <li>Game-based assessments are engaging. Completion rates exceed 90% compared to 60% for traditional aptitude tests</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Custom pricing starts around £5,000/year, excluding small agencies and single-site employers</li>
        <li>Some candidates find video interviews impersonal. The human touch of a phone screen is lost</li>
        <li>AI assessment of facial expressions has faced ethical scrutiny. Ensure transparency with candidates</li>
        <li>Technical requirements (webcam, stable internet) exclude some candidates from disadvantaged backgrounds</li>
        <li>The interface can feel corporate and cold. Brand customisation is limited on lower tiers</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate HireVue 4.3/5 for enterprise recruitment. A Trustpilot reviewer from a retail chain said the on-demand interviews "reduced our time-to-hire from 6 weeks to 10 days." However, several candidates on Glassdoor complained that the AI assessment feels "robotic and dehumanising." Ethical concerns about AI evaluating facial expressions remain prominent in recruitment industry discussions.</p>

      <h3>Pricing</h3>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Essential</td><td>From £5,000/year</td><td>On-demand video, basic assessments, standard support</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Enterprise</td><td>From £15,000/year</td><td>Live interviews, advanced AI assessments, custom branding, dedicated support</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Custom</td><td>Variable</td><td>Volume pricing for high-volume seasonal recruitment</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> Editor's Choice for high-volume and graduate recruitment. HireVue is a significant investment that pays off for organisations hiring at scale. If you recruit fewer than 50 roles per year, the cost is hard to justify. For graduate schemes, retail seasonal hiring, and call centre recruitment, it is transformative.</p>
      <p><a href="https://hirevue.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Request a HireVue demo</a> (affiliate link)</p>

      <h2>4. Occupop</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Healthcare and compliance-heavy recruitment</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.3 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £149/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Occupop is purpose-built for the compliance-intensive world of healthcare staffing. A nursing agency in Liverpool uses it to process 150 applications per month, automatically verifying DBS certificates, right-to-work documents, professional registrations, and training records. The AI features rank candidates by compliance readiness, predict which applicants will complete the onboarding process, and suggest optimal posting strategies for hard-to-fill roles.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI candidate screening:</strong> Parse CVs and rank candidates against job requirements and compliance criteria simultaneously.</li>
        <li><strong>Compliance automation:</strong> Track DBS status, right-to-work documents, NMC registration, training certificates, and mandatory update dates. Automatic alerts prevent lapses.</li>
        <li><strong>Healthcare job board integration:</strong> Post to NHS Jobs, HealthJobsUK, Carehome.co.uk, and specialist healthcare boards from one interface.</li>
        <li><strong>Reference checking:</strong> Automated reference requests with structured, comparable responses. Identify red flags systematically.</li>
        <li><strong>Shift scheduling:</strong> For temporary staffing agencies, match available workers to open shifts based on skills, location, and compliance status.</li>
        <li><strong>Candidate portal:</strong> Applicants upload documents, complete compliance checks, and track their application status in real time.</li>
        <li><strong>Reporting:</strong> CQC-ready reports on recruitment practices, diversity metrics, and compliance status.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The compliance automation is unmatched in healthcare recruitment. One agency eliminated DBS expiry incidents entirely</li>
        <li>Healthcare-specific job board integration saves hours of manual posting</li>
        <li>AI ranking considers compliance readiness, not just skills. No more discovering a perfect candidate lacks right-to-work documents</li>
        <li>The candidate portal reduces admin phone calls by 60%</li>
        <li>CQC-ready reporting demonstrates robust recruitment governance to inspectors</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £149/month, it is expensive for small agencies placing fewer than 20 roles per month</li>
        <li>The interface is functional but utilitarian. Do not expect a polished consumer experience</li>
        <li>AI screening needs calibration for each role type. Initial setup requires investment of time</li>
        <li>Integration with some local authority portals is limited. Expect some manual processes</li>
        <li>Customer support is good but small. Complex issues may take 24-48 hours</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate Occupop 4.2/5 for healthcare recruitment. A Capterra reviewer from a Manchester care agency said the compliance tracking "paid for itself in the first month" by preventing a DBS lapse that would have cost them a contract. Reddit users on r/healthcarerecruitment praise the DBS automation but note the candidate experience is "adequate, not delightful."</p>

      <h3>Pricing</h3>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Starter</td><td>£149/month</td><td>3 active jobs, basic screening, compliance tracking</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Professional</td><td>£299/month</td><td>10 active jobs, AI ranking, multi-posting, analytics</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Enterprise</td><td>Custom</td><td>Unlimited jobs, custom integrations, API access, dedicated support</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> Editor's Choice for healthcare and regulated recruitment. If you recruit nurses, care workers, doctors, or allied health professionals, Occupop's compliance automation is non-negotiable. For generalist recruitment, Workable offers broader features at a similar price.</p>
      <p><a href="https://occupop.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start an Occupop trial</a> (affiliate link)</p>

      <h2>5. Greenhouse</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Structured hiring, DEI focus, and enterprise applicant tracking</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.6 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Custom pricing (typically £200-£400/month for small teams)</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>Greenhouse built its reputation on structured hiring: the methodology that reduces bias and improves hiring accuracy by standardising every step of the process. A tech scale-up in London uses it to ensure every candidate experiences the same assessment criteria, interview questions, and evaluation rubrics. The AI features suggest interview questions based on role requirements, analyse job descriptions for biased language, and predict which sourcing channels deliver the best candidates.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Structured hiring framework:</strong> Standardised scorecards, interview plans, and evaluation criteria for every role. Ensure consistency and compliance.</li>
        <li><strong>AI job description analysis:</strong> Scan your job descriptions for biased language, gender-coded terms, and accessibility issues before posting.</li>
        <li><strong>Interview question suggestions:</strong> AI generates role-specific, competency-based interview questions aligned to your scorecard criteria.</li>
        <li><strong>Candidate sourcing:</strong> Integrates with LinkedIn, Indeed, and niche job boards. Track source effectiveness and cost-per-hire by channel.</li>
        <li><strong>Offer management:</strong> Generate offers, manage approvals, and track acceptance rates. Analyse which factors influence candidate decisions.</li>
        <li><strong>DEI analytics:</strong> Track diversity metrics at every stage of the funnel. Identify where underrepresented candidates drop out and why.</li>
        <li><strong>Extensive integrations:</strong> 300+ integrations including Slack, Zoom, Workday, and BambooHR.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The structured hiring methodology genuinely reduces bias. One client increased diversity in senior hires by 40%</li>
        <li>Job description analysis catches biased language that hiring managers miss</li>
        <li>The scorecard system ensures every interviewer assesses the same competencies</li>
        <li>DEI analytics provide the data to hold leadership accountable for diversity goals</li>
        <li>The integration ecosystem is the most extensive in the ATS market</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Pricing is opaque and starts around £200/month, making it expensive for small agencies</li>
        <li>The interface is powerful but complex. Expect significant training investment</li>
        <li>Some users report the AI question suggestions are generic and need customisation</li>
        <li>Advanced features (offer management, DEI analytics) require higher-tier plans</li>
        <li>Customer support is excellent for enterprise clients but less responsive for smaller accounts</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What Users Say</h3>
      <p>G2 reviewers rate Greenhouse 4.5/5, calling it "the gold standard for structured hiring." A Trustpilot reviewer from a London fintech company said the DEI analytics "gave us the data to finally address our diversity problem." The main complaint: the cost and complexity make it unsuitable for agencies with fewer than 10 concurrent roles.</p>

      <h3>Pricing</h3>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Plan</th><th>Price</th><th>What you get</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Essential</td><td>From £200/month</td><td>Core ATS, basic reporting, standard integrations</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Advanced</td><td>From £400/month</td><td>Structured hiring, DEI analytics, advanced reporting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Expert</td><td>Custom</td><td>Enterprise security, custom workflows, dedicated support</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Verdict:</strong> Also Great for structured hiring and DEI-focused organisations. Greenhouse is the platform of choice for companies that take hiring methodology seriously. If you are committed to reducing bias and improving hiring accuracy, the investment pays off. For transactional recruitment agencies, simpler tools may be more efficient.</p>
