      <h2>7. TestGorilla</h2>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Skills testing, cognitive assessments, and bias reduction</p>
      <p><strong>Star rating:</strong> 4.4 / 5</p>
      <p><strong>Starting price:</strong> Approx £59/month</p>

      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>TestGorilla replaces gut feeling with data in the screening process. A Leeds software company uses it to test every developer candidate on coding skills, problem-solving ability, and communication before the first interview. The result: interview time reduced by 60%, and hiring accuracy improved because only genuinely qualified candidates reach the interview stage.</p>

      <h3>Key Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>250+ pre-built tests:</strong> Programming, languages, cognitive ability, personality, situational judgment, and role-specific skills.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom test builder:</strong> Create your own assessments tailored to your company's specific requirements and culture.</li>
        <li><strong>Anti-cheating measures:</strong> Webcam proctoring, question randomisation, and time limits ensure assessment integrity.</li>
        <li><strong>Candidate experience:</strong> Mobile-friendly tests with clear instructions and immediate feedback. Respect applicants' time.</li>
        <li><strong>ATS integration:</strong> Connects with Workable, Greenhouse, BambooHR, and most major platforms. Scores flow automatically into candidate records.</li>
        <li><strong>Diversity analytics:</strong> Track assessment completion rates and score distributions by demographic group. Identify barriers in your process.</li>
        <li><strong>Skills benchmarking:</strong> Compare candidate scores against global averages and your previous hires.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Pros</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The test library is comprehensive. From Python coding to customer service simulations, there is a test for almost any role</li>
        <li>Anti-cheating measures are robust. Proctoring and randomisation maintain assessment integrity</li>
        <li>Custom tests let you assess culture fit and company-specific knowledge</li>
        <li>Skills benchmarking provides context. A "good" score means more when compared to global data</li>
        <li>The candidate experience is respectful. Tests are concise, clear, and mobile-friendly</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Cons</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>At £59/month, it is an additional cost on top of your ATS</li>
        <li>Some tests feel generic. Highly specialised roles may need custom assessment development</li>
        <li>Candidates with test anxiety may underperform despite being qualified. Balance testing with other evaluation methods</li>
        <li>The interface is functional but not inspiring. Expect a utilitarian experience</li>
        <li>Some users report occasional technical issues with video proctoring on older devices</li>
      </ul>

